1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,710
Did you get through to your mother?

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:10,320
Yes. She made me promise to eat after this.

3
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:16,450
If you need more time, we can talk in private.

4
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,180
No. You keep those. I'll answer.

5
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:32,310
Let her finish the question. If you don't understand, ask.

6
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,020
Okay.

7
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:51,330
Do you swear that your answers to the court will be truthful?

8
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,260
I do.

9
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:58,340
If you don't understand a question, tell me.

10
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:13,520
These charges permit a life sentence. Has anyone promised a sentence, or promised that New York will dismiss its case?

11
00:01:14,170 --> 00:01:19,130
No. I understand. Nobody's promised me either of those.

12
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:28,900
How do you plead to interstate stalking resulting in death, and cyberstalking resulting in death?

13
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:31,880
Guilty on both counts.

14
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:53,200
I went online to find out where Brian Ward would be. I traveled from another state to New York to follow him. I intended to kill him.

15
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:04,900
Did you understand your conduct would place him in fear of death or serious injury?

16
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:11,030
Yes. I shot him. He died because I shot him.

17
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:23,850
I still object to what the industry does. That doesn't change my answers.

18
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:29,460
The pleas are accepted. Sentencing will be set separately.

19
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,130
Was this his decision?

20
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:47,410
Yes. He wanted to speak for himself. We've filed in state court. This is the receipt.

21
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:57,210
The state says these are different harms, so they can prosecute. Could the plea still stop them?

22
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:05,760
That's for the judge. We haven't had a ruling.

23
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:13,460
Get the date in too. It's a filing receipt. Nobody's ordered his release.
